## SCSS/Sass

### When to Use SCSS
Use SCSS for:
- Complex styling beyond Tailwind
- Animations and transitions
- Pseudo-elements (::before, ::after)
- Complex selectors
- SCSS variables and mixins

### Component Styles
```vue
<template>
  <view class="custom-component">
    <text class="title">Title</text>
  </view>
</template>

<style scoped lang="scss">
.custom-component {
  position: relative;
  
  .title {
    font-size: 32rpx;
    
    &::after {
      content: '';
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: 2rpx;
      background: linear-gradient(to right, #667eea, #764ba2);
    }
  }
}
</style>
```

### Global Styles (uni.scss)
```scss
// /src/uni.scss
$uni-color-primary: #007AFF;
$uni-color-success: #4CD964;
$uni-font-size-base: 28rpx;
$uni-spacing-base: 20rpx;
```

Use in components:
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
@import '@/uni.scss';

.button {
  background-color: $uni-color-primary;
  font-size: $uni-font-size-base;
}
</style>
```

### Animations
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
.fade-in {
  animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease-in;
}

@keyframes fadeIn {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(20rpx);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}
</style>
```

### Transitions
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
.hover-card {
  transition: all 0.3s ease;
  
  &:active {
    transform: scale(0.98);
    opacity: 0.8;
  }
}
</style>
```

### Gradients
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
.gradient-bg {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
}
</style>
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Prefer Tailwind
```vue
<!-- ✅ Good - Tailwind -->
<view class="flex items-center p-[20rpx] bg-white rounded-lg">
  <text class="text-[28rpx] font-medium">Title</text>
</view>

<!-- ❌ Bad - Unnecessary custom CSS -->
<view class="custom-container">
  <text class="custom-title">Title</text>
</view>

<style>
.custom-container { /* ... */ }
.custom-title { /* ... */ }
</style>
```

### 2. Use rpx
```vue
<!-- ✅ Good - rpx -->
<view class="w-[750rpx] h-[200rpx]">

<!-- ❌ Bad - px -->
<view class="w-[375px] h-[100px]">
```

### 3. Use Scoped Styles
```vue
<!-- ✅ Good -->
<style scoped lang="scss">
.container { }
</style>

<!-- ❌ Bad - affects other components -->
<style lang="scss">
.container { }
</style>
```

### 4. Avoid Deep Selectors
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
// ✅ Good
.container {
  > .item {
    margin: 10rpx;
  }
}

// ⚠️ Use sparingly
.container {
  :deep(.uni-input) {
    font-size: 28rpx;
  }
}
</style>
```

### 5. Mobile-First Responsive
```vue
<!-- ✅ Good - mobile first -->
<view class="p-[20rpx] sm:p-[40rpx] md:p-[60rpx]">

<!-- ❌ Bad - desktop first -->
<view class="p-[60rpx] md:p-[40rpx] sm:p-[20rpx]">
```

## Common Styling Patterns

### Safe Area (iPhone notch)
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
.page-with-safe-area {
  padding-top: constant(safe-area-inset-top);
  padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);
  
  padding-bottom: constant(safe-area-inset-bottom);
  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
}
</style>
```

### Fixed Footer
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
.footer {
  position: fixed;
  bottom: 0;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  padding: 20rpx;
  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
  background: white;
  box-shadow: 0 -2rpx 10rpx rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
}
</style>
```

### Ellipsis Text
```vue
<style scoped lang="scss">
// Single line
.ellipsis-single {
  overflow: hidden;
  white-space: nowrap;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

// Multi-line
.ellipsis-multi {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
  overflow: hidden;
}
</style>
```

## Performance

1. **Minimize custom styles** - Use Tailwind when possible
2. **Avoid complex selectors** - Keep < 3 levels deep
3. **Use CSS variables** - Better for theming
4. **Optimize animations** - Use `transform` and `opacity`
5. **Avoid layout thrashing** - Batch DOM reads/writes
